in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @kintsugi
in @kintsugi/consent

# @kintsugi/morphism — the typed pre/post-morphism pair sub-shard;
# the per-candidate eigenboard.context slice that lifts the substrate's
# `pre_anchor` data from realisation-layer seam to substrate-altitude
# declaration.
#
# THE T14.1 SUB-SHARD landing the forward-promise consent.mirror named
# eight ticks ago. Lines 138-146 of `consent.mirror` (the substrate gap
# surfaced honestly):
#
#   "Substrate gap (surfaced honestly): the substrate has no `morphism`
#    carrier at @mirror or @glass altitude — the term was always relative
#    (refract.mirror talks about morphisms on the eigenboard; au.mirror
#    talks about proposed compositions; @mirror/spectral talks about
#    coordination morphisms). This shard declares the SPECIFIC morphism
#    shape the auto-apply boundary needs: a candidate with an expected
#    trajectory. A future @kintsugi/morphism sub-shard MAY lift
#    this to a more general morphism type; consent's load is the
#    auto-apply case."
#
# This shard lands that lift — additively, without modifying
# consent.mirror's (FROZEN-adjacent) `type morphism`. consent's narrower
# carrier stays the consent-altitude per-candidate observation unit;
# this shard declares the morphism-altitude per-candidate context
# carrier that pairs each candidate morphism with its pre-anchor ref.
#
# Load-bearing spec: docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md §4.7 (the consent
# surface formalisation; identity_preserving reads DARK bits of the
# PRE-morphism vs POST-morphism shard; the comparison requires the
# pre-anchor as a typed substrate datum, not an opaque ref hiding in
# the loop driver's state).
#
# === The recognition: the substrate had already named the pair at the
# orchestra altitude (the 25th-instance candidate) ===
#
# Three prior ticks built every primitive this shard composes:
#
#   @kintsugi/consent               the morphism carrier;        (c3802eba)
#                                    the consent-altitude
#                                    per-candidate observation
#                                    (type morphism = { content,
#                                    score, expected })
#   @kintsugi/oscillate             the oscillation carrier;     (-)
#                                    type oscillation = { state,
#                                    iteration, anchor: ref } —
#                                    the loop holds the anchor
#                                    STABLE across passes; the
#                                    pre_anchor data was always in
#                                    the loop driver's per-tick state
#   @mirror/spectral/score          the orchestra-altitude pair;  (-)
#                                    type score = { anchor: ref,
#                                    session: metalogue_session,
#                                    pending: morphism_set } —
#                                    the WHOLE-orchestra eigenboard
#                                    context: an anchor paired with
#                                    a set of pending morphisms
#
# The substrate had been quietly carrying (anchor, morphism_set) pairs
# at THREE altitudes:
#
#   - oscillate altitude:  oscillation.anchor + the loop's implicit
#                          per-tick pending morphisms (still implicit)
#   - score altitude:      score.anchor + score.pending (typed; the
#                          orchestra's shared-score reading)
#   - consent altitude:    NO anchor; query_phi(candidates) reads
#                          morphism_set in isolation — THIS IS THE GAP
#
# What was missing: the PER-CANDIDATE slice of the orchestra-altitude
# pair. score's `{ anchor, pending }` is the WHOLE orchestra's
# context; query_phi needs each candidate paired with its pre-anchor
# so identity_preserving(m) can compare DARK bits across the morphism.
# This shard declares that per-candidate slice.
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (now the 25th
# recognition): each "missing concept" turns out to be a name the
# substrate was already implicitly using. The pre_anchor data was at
# the oscillation altitude (in the loop's state) AND at the score
# altitude (as the anchor field). The per-candidate altitude was the
# only gap.
#
# === The morphism-altitude per-candidate context ===
#
# `morphism_context` carries:
#
#   pre_anchor   — the substrate ref BEFORE the morphism is applied.
#                   The anchor shard handle whose uuid_spectral's DARK
#                   80 bits identity_preserving reads to compare against
#                   the morphism's resulting shard. Per @uuid/spectral's
#                   void duality: ACTIVE 48 bits may shift (the
#                   navigable spectral coordinate re-routes as the
#                   morphism applies); DARK 80 bits MUST be preserved
#                   (the identity_preserving gate). pre_anchor is what
#                   identity_preserving compares against.
#   candidate    — the morphism (per `@kintsugi/consent`'s
#                   `type morphism = { content, score, expected }`).
#                   The candidate morphism's content ref carries the
#                   POST-morphism shard handle; the comparison is
#                   pre_anchor.uuid.dark ?= candidate.content.uuid.dark.
#
# A `morphism_context` lifts a `consent::morphism` by adding the
# `pre_anchor: ref` field. The realisation layer projects:
#
#   morphism_context → morphism  via `candidate` field (drop pre_anchor;
#                                 narrow to consent altitude)
#   morphism_context → ref pair  via `{ pre_anchor, candidate.content }`
#                                 (the DARK-bits comparison's two
#                                 operands)
#
# Both projections are substrate-honest; the morphism_context carries
# both observations as a single typed record.
#
# === The morphism-context-set carrier ===
#
# `morphism_context_set = [morphism_context]` is the family-altitude
# lift of consent.mirror's `morphism_set = [morphism]`. Per
# dissonance.mirror's `pareto_set = [candidate]` precedent: list-of-type
# form at declaration position is substrate-accepted.
#
# Symmetry note: a morphism_context_set projects to a
# consent::morphism_set (drop the pre_anchor field per the
# morphism_context → morphism projection above) when the consent-
# altitude reading is needed; the substrate carries both shapes so the
# dispatch is honest at each altitude.
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `@kintsugi/consent`, `morphism` is the consent-altitude
# per-candidate carrier; this shard re-uses it (pulled into scope via
# `in @kintsugi/consent` above). Per `glass.mirror`, `ref` is
# the substrate's reference floor. Per the `_context` suffix precedent
# (eigenboard.context referenced in consent.mirror, oscillate.mirror,
# and score.mirror as the substrate's vocabulary for the
# pre-pulse environment a morphism is evaluated in), `morphism_context`
# names the per-candidate slice of that context.
#
# This shard declares `morphism_context` as a record per the
# pause_event / score precedent; `morphism_context_set =
# [morphism_context]` as a list-of-type per the pareto_set /
# morphism_set precedent; the `paired` constructor action returning
# `morphism_context`. NO new verdict carrier; NO leading-`|`
# workarounds; NO opaque-`ref` carriers where structured types are
# available (per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]).
#
# === The relationship to score.mirror ===
#
# `score.mirror`'s `type score = { anchor: ref, session,
# pending: morphism_set }` declares the WHOLE-orchestra eigenboard
# context. This shard's `morphism_context = { pre_anchor: ref,
# candidate: morphism }` declares the PER-CANDIDATE slice. The two
# compose:
#
#   to_contexts(s: score) -> morphism_context_set =
#     [ paired(s.anchor, m) | m in s.pending ]
#
# (The substrate names the obligation; the projection itself stays
# obligation-blocked. T15 may substrate-declare to_contexts as a
# typed action; this tick names only the per-candidate carrier.)
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
#   - The pre_anchor reads a single substrate ref; the substrate has no
#     "anchor history" carrier at this altitude. A morphism applied to
#     an anchor that has itself been morphed N steps ago compares
#     against the IMMEDIATE pre-anchor, not the original. This is
#     substrate-fact, not a gap: identity_preserving rides the per-pulse
#     DARK-bits check; longer-horizon identity questions belong to the
#     @uuid/spectral altitude (the navigable spectral coordinate's
#     history), not to morphism_context.
#
#   - The `candidate.content` ref carries the POST-morphism shard handle
#     OPTIMISTICALLY — the realisation layer reads `candidate.content`
#     as "what the morphism would produce if applied"; the
#     identity_preserving gate decides whether the application happens.
#     The substrate names the shape; the optimism / discharge sequence
#     is the realisation layer's concern.
#
# === Forward-promise to T15 (the consumer-pull tick) ===
#
# After this shard lands, T15 has a typed substrate datum to lift
# query_phi's signature to. Two paths are open:
#
#   A. query_phi gains a context parameter:
#        query_phi(candidates: morphism_context_set) -> verdict
#      — the consent surface reads each candidate's pre_anchor;
#      identity_preserving's body compares DARK bits against the typed
#      pre_anchor rather than reaching through an opaque sibling ref.
#
#   B. query_phi's signature stays unchanged; identity_preserving's
#      body gains an internal `morphism_context` synthesis from the
#      score the consumer passes adjacent. The consent surface reads
#      score → morphism_context_set via the to_contexts composition;
#      query_phi composes per-candidate from there.
#
# Path A is the substrate-pull-honest lift (the parameter becomes
# substrate-fact rather than realisation-layer plumbing); path B
# preserves consent.mirror's signature stability. T15 picks per the
# substrate-pull discipline; this shard names only the carrier.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
# Every type below names an established object older than the
# discipline of computer science:
#
#   morphism context   Eilenberg & Mac Lane (1945) "General theory of
#                       natural equivalences"; the (source, arrow)
#                       observation unit — a morphism with its
#                       domain explicitly named. The category-theoretic
#                       arrow IS the pair (object, arrow-from-object);
#                       this shard names that pair at substrate altitude.
#   pre/post duality   the categorical duality of (id_A → f) vs
#                       (f → id_B) — the identity-on-source vs
#                       identity-on-target reading of a morphism's
#                       endpoints. The substrate's pre_anchor is the
#                       id_A reading; the candidate.content ref is the
#                       implicit id_B reading.
#   pair               Wiener (1914) / Kuratowski (1921); the ordered
#                       pair as the foundational data structure. The
#                       morphism_context IS an ordered pair (anchor,
#                       morphism); the constructor `paired` names it.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* the pair so the formatter
# reads it. No invention.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md §4.7 (the consent surface
#               formalisation; identity_preserving requires the
#               pre-morphism DARK bits as a comparison operand),
#               docs/specs/kintsugi-tournament.md §3 (the gate+rank
#               pipeline; identity_preserving is one of the three gates).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (the lift
#                      from realisation-layer plumbing to substrate-
#                      altitude declaration is the substrate-pull
#                      gradient — the substrate-pull always wants the
#                      typed carrier),
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                      (pre_anchor is substrate vocabulary; declared
#                      in the shard; the realisation layer reads the
#                      typed carrier rather than threading an opaque
#                      ref through query_phi's sibling parameter),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (morphism_context is
#                      its own carrier; the pre_anchor + candidate pair
#                      does NOT escape as a bare tuple-of-refs).
# Substrate recognitions: [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the 25th-instance recognition; the substrate
#                      had been carrying anchor-morphism pairs at the
#                      oscillation altitude AND at the score altitude
#                      for ticks before query_phi's realisation surfaced
#                      the per-candidate gap),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull]] (no invention; the
#                      shape is the additive lift of consent's
#                      morphism by score's anchor pattern).
# Forward-promise to consumers: T15 (`query_phi` signature lift, OR
#                  `identity_preserving` body composition) consumes
#                  this carrier; the binding lands when T15
#                  substrate-pulls. This shard does NOT pull
#                  `@mirror/spectral/score` or `@kintsugi/oscillate`;
#                  the substrate-altitude arrow points
#                  inward (morphism_context IS consumed by consent's
#                  query_phi / by identity_preserving; not the other
#                  way around).
# Related shards: mirror/spectral.mirror (the family root; declares
#                 this sub-shard as the per-candidate context species),
#                 mirror/spectral/consent.mirror (the consent altitude;
#                 `morphism` is re-used here as the candidate field;
#                 `query_phi` is the load-bearing consumer T15 lifts),
#                 mirror/spectral/score.mirror (the orchestra altitude;
#                 `score.anchor` IS the same data as `morphism_context.
#                 pre_anchor` at a different altitude; the per-candidate
#                 lift of the orchestra-altitude pair),
#                 mirror/spectral/oscillate.mirror (the loop driver;
#                 `oscillation.anchor` IS the same data again at the
#                 loop altitude; the substrate has been carrying the
#                 anchor at three altitudes and this shard lands the
#                 per-candidate fourth),
#                 uuid/spectral.mirror (the DARK-bits comparison that
#                 identity_preserving rides; `dark(pre_anchor.uuid)`
#                 vs `dark(candidate.content.uuid)`).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/kintsugi/morphism.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/morphism` as a species under the `@kintsugi`
# family. Migrated from `@mirror/spectral/morphism` 2026-06-10
# per the form/process partition (recognition #55 candidate;
# the typed pre/post-morphism pair is process-side — it
# describes the per-candidate transformation slice).

glass @kintsugi/morphism {
  focus morphism
  project morphism
  split morphism
  shift morphism
  settle morphism
}

# === The morphism-context carrier ===
#
# The per-candidate slice of the eigenboard.context. Pairs each
# candidate morphism with its pre-anchor — the substrate ref BEFORE
# the morphism is applied. The carrier identity_preserving(m) reads
# to compare DARK 80 bits across the morphism boundary.
#
# pre_anchor  — substrate ref to the pre-morphism shard handle (the
#                anchor the kintsugi loop is currently positioned on).
#                Read by identity_preserving as the LHS of the
#                @uuid/spectral.dark byte-equality check.
# candidate   — the morphism the formatter is proposing to apply
#                (per `@kintsugi/consent`'s `morphism` carrier).
#                Its `content` ref carries the POST-morphism shard
#                handle (optimistic; the apply happens only if the
#                gates pass); its `score` and `expected` fields carry
#                the dissonance + cadence readings for the discriminator.
#
# Identity contract: two morphism_contexts are equal iff their
# pre_anchor and candidate fields both match. The realisation layer
# enforces.
type morphism_context = {
  pre_anchor: ref,
  candidate:  morphism,
}

# === The morphism-context-set carrier ===
#
# The set of candidate morphism_contexts the consent surface evaluates
# at a given oscillation tick. The family-altitude lift of
# consent.mirror's `morphism_set` — each candidate now carries its
# pre-anchor so identity_preserving's DARK-bits comparison is
# self-contained.
#
# Per dissonance.mirror's `pareto_set = [candidate]` precedent:
# list-of-type form at declaration position is substrate-accepted.
#
# Symmetry note: a morphism_context_set projects to a consent's
# `morphism_set` (drop the pre_anchor field per the morphism_context →
# morphism projection) when the consent-altitude reading is needed;
# the substrate carries both shapes so the dispatch is honest at each
# altitude. The realisation layer projects.
#
# Identity contract: two morphism_context_sets are equal iff their
# morphism_context sequences are element-wise equal. The realisation
# layer enforces.
type morphism_context_set = [morphism_context]

# === paired — the constructor ===
#
# Constructs a typed morphism_context from a pre-anchor ref and a
# candidate morphism. The substrate's canonical pair-construction
# action; consumers compose pre/post pairs through this carrier rather
# than through ad-hoc tuple-of-refs threading.
#
# Composes through:
#
#   1. Direct field assignment: `{ pre_anchor: pre, candidate: m }`.
#      No computation; the constructor IS the record construction.
#
# Consumers:
#
#   - T15's `query_phi` signature lift reads `paired` to construct
#     morphism_context_set from (anchor, morphism_set) pairs. The
#     consent surface composes:
#       morphism_context_set = [ paired(score.anchor, m)
#                              | m in score.pending ]
#     — the orchestra-altitude `(anchor, pending)` becomes the
#     per-candidate `morphism_context_set` via this constructor.
#
#   - The kintsugi loop's `pulse` reads `paired` when composing the
#     candidate-set query_phi reads: each pulse's pre_anchor is
#     `oscillation.anchor`; each candidate is one element of the
#     active_pass-emitted morphism_set; the constructor pairs them.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads
# `pre` and `m`, emits the two-field record. The substrate names the
# constructor; the arithmetic IS the record construction.
paired(pre: ref, m: morphism) -> morphism_context { \ }

out @kintsugi/morphism
out morphism_context
out morphism_context_set
out paired
